y: [Each new hire assigned a buddy — role/name]\nProductivity ramp assumption: [e.g., 50% capacity in weeks 1-2; 75% in weeks 3-4; 100% from week 5]\n\n---\n\n10. BUDGET SUMMARY:\n| Role | Type | Count | Monthly Cost (est.) | Period | Total Cost |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [Role] | Permanent | [N] | [Cost] | [N months] | [Total] |\n| [Role] | Contractor | [N] | [Cost] | [N months] | [Total] |\n\n| Cost Category | Amount | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| Permanent headcount | [Cost] | [N roles x N months] |\n| Contractor augmentation | [Cost] | [N roles x N months] |\n| Recruitment fees | [Cost] | [e.g., 15-20% of first year salary per hire] |\n| Onboarding and tooling | [Cost] | [e.g., Licences, equipment] |\n| TOTAL | [Cost] | [Planning period stated in CONTEXT] |\n\nBudget vs approved headcount: [On budget | Over by [N] | Under by [N] — action required?]
