y | Date Raised | Owner | Target Resolution |\n\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n\n| I-01 | [Description] | [Role] | [DD/MM/YYYY] | [Role] | [DD/MM/YYYY] |\n\n \n\n---\n\n \n\n9. GOVERNANCE AND COMMUNICATION PLAN:\n\nMeetings:\n\n| Meeting | Frequency | Attendees | Owner | Output |\n\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n\n| Daily Standup | Daily | Engineering team | Tech Lead | Blocker log |\n\n| Sprint Review | Bi-weekly | Team + PO | PM | Sprint summary |\n\n| Stakeholder Update | Weekly | Sponsor + PM | PM | WSR |\n\n| Steering Committee | Monthly | Sponsor + leads | PM | Escalation decisions |\n\n \n\nReporting:\n\n  - [e.g., "Weekly Status Report (WSR) distributed every Friday by PM"]\n\n  - [e.g., "RAG status updated in project tracker every Monday morning"]\n\n \n\nEscalation Path:\n\n  - Level 1 — Blocker within team: [e.g., Tech Lead resolves within 24hrs]\n\n  - Level 2 — Cross-team or resource conflict: [e.g., PM escalates within 48hrs]\n\n  - Level 3 — Scope, budget, or timeline impact: [e.g., Sponsor decision within 72hrs]\n\n \n\nChange Control:\n\n  - [e.g., "Any in-scope change request requires PM + PO sign-off before work begins"]\n\n  - [e.g., "Changes impacting Go-Live date require Sponsor approval"]\n\n \n\n---\n\n \n\n10. CRITICAL PATH:\n\n \n\n⚠️ CRITICAL PATH TASKS:\n\n| Task ID | Task Description | Owner | Duration | Why Critical |\n\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n\n| [T-N.N] | [Description] | [Role] | [X days] | [What breaks if this is delayed] |\n\n \n\nCritical Path Summary:\n\n  [Phase 1 key task] → [Phase 2 key task] → [Phase 3 key task] → [Go-Live Milestone]\n\n  Total critical path duration: [X weeks / days]\n\n  Float available: [X days — or "Zero float — any slip delays Go-Live"]\n\n \n\n---\n\n \n\nPLAN SUMMARY:\n\nTOTAL PHASES: [N]\n\nTOTAL TASKS: [N]\n\nTOTAL MILESTONES: [N]\n\nTASKS WITHOUT OWNERS: [N] — IDs: [list or 'None']\n\nCRITICAL PATH TASKS: [N] — IDs: [list]\n\nASSUMPTIONS MADE: [N]\n\nOPEN RISKS: [N] | ESCALATED: [N]\n\nOPEN ISSUES: [N]\n\nRESOURCE GAPS: [N]\n\nNEEDS CLARIFICATION FLAGS: [N] — Topics: [list]
19	5	API design prompts	ROLE:\nYou are a senior Software Engineer specializing in API design for web,\nmobile backend, and microservice systems.\n\nCONTEXT:\nProject: [Project Name]\nPlatform: iOS | Android | Web | All\nAPI Type: REST | GraphQL | gRPC | WebSocket | tRPC\nAuthentication: JWT | OAuth 2.0 | API Key | Session | None\nConsumers: Mobile app | Web frontend | Third-party | Internal services | All\nDatabase: PostgreSQL | MySQL | MongoDB | Redis | [Other]\nTech Stack: [e.g., Node.js | FastAPI | Django | Spring Boot | [Other]]\nScale: [e.g., MVP | 10k req/day | 1M req/day]\n\nTASK:\nUsing the feature requirements and system context provided below, produce a\ncomplete API design with all endpoints, contracts, and implementation guidance.\n\nYou MUST cover ALL of the following — do not skip any:\n  1. API structure — resource naming, URL conventions, and versioning strategy\n  2. Endpoint design — every endpoint with method, path, purpose, and ownership\n  3. Request contracts — headers, path params, query params, and request body for every endpoint\n  4. Response contracts — success and error response schemas for every endpoint\n  5. Authentication and authorisation — how each endpoint is secured\n  6. Validation rules — field-level validation for every input field\n  7. Error handling — complete error taxonomy with codes, messages, and HTTP status\n  8. Pagination and filtering — strategy for list endpoints\n  9. Rate limiting — limits per endpoint tier and handling of limit exceeded\n  10. Versioning and deprecation — how breaking changes are managed\n\nEvaluate the FULL feature requirements before designing any endpoint.\nEvery design decision must include a justification.\nDo NOT design endpoints that are not required by the stated features.\nFlag any requirement that is ambiguous as [NEEDS CLARIFICATION] — never assume.\n\nFEATURE REQUIREMENTS AND SYSTEM CONTEXT:\n[Paste feature list, data models, consumer requirements, and any existing API context here]\n\nCONSTRAINTS:\n- Resource names must be plural nouns — never verbs in REST endpoints\n- Every endpoint must handle all relevant HTTP status codes — not just 200\n- Validation rules must be precise — no vague constraints like "must be valid"\n- Breaking changes must be versioned — never silently change an existing contract\n- Response envelopes must be consistent across all endpoints\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\nAPI DESIGN DOCUMENT\nProject: [Project Name] | API Type: [Type] | Version: v[N]\nPrepared By: [Engineer Name] | Date: [DD/MM/YYYY]\nBase URL: [e.g., https://api.projectname.com/v1]\n\n---\n\n1. API STRUCTURE:\nResource naming convention: [e.g., Plural nouns — /users | /orders | /products]\nURL structure: /v{version}/{resource}/{id}/{sub-resource}\nVersioning strategy: URL path versioning — /v1/ | /v2/\nHTTP methods:\n  GET    — Read resource(s) — never mutate state\n  POST   — Create new resource\n  PUT    — Full replace of existing resource\n  PATCH  — Partial update of existing resource\n  DELETE — Remove resource\n\n---\n\n2. ENDPOINT DESIGN:\n| Method | Path | Purpose | Auth Required | Consumer |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| GET | /[resource] | List all [resources] with pagination | Yes/No | [Consumer] |\n| GET | /[resource]/{id} | Get single [resource] by ID | Yes/No | [Consumer] |\n| POST | /[resource] | Create new [resource] | Yes/No | [Consumer] |\n| PUT | /[resource]/{id} | Replace [resource] | Yes/No | [Consumer] |\n| PATCH | /[resource]/{id} | Partially update [resource] | Yes/No | [Consumer] |\n| DELETE | /[resource]/{id} | Delete [resource] | Yes/No | [Consumer] |\n\n---\n(repeat for every resource)\n\n---\n\n3. REQUEST CONTRACTS:\n\nENDPOINT: [METHOD] [PATH]\nHeaders:\n| Header | Required | Value |\n|---|---|---|\n| Authorization | Yes | Bearer {token} |\n| Content-Type | Yes | application/json |\n| [Header] | Yes/No | [Value] |\n\nPath Parameters:\n| Parameter | Type | Required | Description | Example |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| id | uuid | Yes | Unique resource identifier | 550e8400-e29b-41d4-a716 |\n\nQuery Parameters (list endpoints):\n| Parameter | Type | Required | Default | Description | Example |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| page | integer | No | 1 | Page number | 1 |\n| limit | integer | No | 20 | Items per page — max 100 | 20 |\n| sort | string | No | created_at | Sort field | created_at |\n| order | string | No | desc | asc or desc | desc |\n| [filter] | [type] | No | [default] | [description] | [example] |\n\nRequest Body:\n| Field | Type | Required | Constraints | Description |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [field] | string | Yes | Min 1, Max 255 chars | [Description] |\n| [field] | integer | No | Min 0, Max 999999 | [Description] |\n| [field] | boolean | No | — | [Description] |\n\n---\n(repeat for every endpoint)\n\n---\n\n4. RESPONSE CONTRACTS:\n\nSuccess response envelope (all endpoints):\n{\n  "success": true,\n  "data": { } or [ ],\n  "meta": {\n    "timestamp": "ISO8601",\n    "version": "v1",\n    "requestId": "uuid"\n  }\n}\n\nPaginated list response:\n{\n  "success": true,\n  "data": [ ],\n  "pagination": {\n    "page": 1,\n    "limit": 20,\n    "total": 100,\n    "totalPages": 5,\n    "hasNext": true,\n    "hasPrev": false\n  }\n}\n\nENDPOINT: [METHOD] [PATH] — Success [200/201]:\n{\n  "success": true,\n  "data": {\n    "[field]": "[type — description]",\n    "[field]": "[type — description]"\n  }\n}\n\n---\n(repeat for every endpoint)\n\n---\n\n5. AUTHENTICATION AND AUTHORISATION:\nStrategy: JWT Bearer token | OAuth 2.0 | API Key\nToken format: [Description]\nToken expiry: Access: [X min] | Refresh: [X days]\n\nEndpoint permission matrix:\n| Endpoint | Public | Authenticated User | Admin | Service Account |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| GET /[resource] | ✅/❌ | ✅/❌ | ✅/❌ | ✅/❌ |\n| POST /[resource] | ✅/❌ | ✅/❌ | ✅/❌ | ✅/❌ |\n| DELETE /[resource]/{id} | ❌ | ✅/❌ | ✅ | ✅/❌ |\n\n---\n\n6. VALIDATION RULES:\n| Field | Type | Required | Min | Max | Pattern | Custom Rule |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [field] | string | Yes | 1 char | 255 chars | [regex — or N/A] | [Custom rule — or N/A] |\n| email | string | Yes | — | 254 chars | RFC 5322 email format | Must be unique per user |\n| [field] | integer | No | 0 | 999999 | — | [Custom rule] |\n\nValidation error response:\n{\n  "success": false,\n  "error": {\n    "code": "VALIDATION_ERROR",\n    "message": "Request validation failed",\n    "details": [\n      {\n        "field": "[field name]",\n        "message": "[Human readable validation message]",\n        "value": "[Rejected value]"\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n\n---\n\n7. ERROR HANDLING:\nError response envelope (all errors):\n{\n  "success": false,\n  "error": {\n    "code": "[ERROR_CODE]",\n    "message": "[Human readable message — safe for client display]",\n    "details": { },\n    "requestId": "uuid"\n  }\n}\n\nError taxonomy:\n| HTTP Status | Error Code | Meaning | Cause | Client Action |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 400 | VALIDATION_ERROR | Request failed validation | Invalid field values | Fix request per details array |\n| 401 | UNAUTHORIZED | Authentication required | Missing or expired token | Re-authenticate |\n| 403 | FORBIDDEN | Insufficient permissions | Valid token, wrong role | Request access or contact admin |\n| 404 | NOT_FOUND | Resource not found | Invalid ID or deleted resource | Check ID and retry |\n| 409 | CONFLICT | Resource conflict | Duplicate unique field | Check for existing resource |\n| 422 | UNPROCESSABLE | Business rule violation | [Specific rule] | [Client guidance] |\n| 429 | RATE_LIMIT_EXCEEDED | Too many requests | Rate limit reached | Retry after X-RateLimit-Reset |\n| 500 | INTERNAL_ERROR | Server error | Unexpected failure | Retry with exponential backoff |\n| 503 | SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE | Service temporarily down | Maintenance or overload | Retry after Retry-After header |\n\n---\n\n8. PAGINATION AND FILTERING:\nStrategy: Offset-based | Cursor-based — justification: [Why]\n\nList endpoint standard params:\n  page, limit, sort, order — on all list endpoints\n  Filters: [List of supported filter params per resource]\n\nCursor-based (if chosen):\n  Request:  ?cursor=[opaque_cursor]&limit=20\n  Response: { "nextCursor": "[value]", "hasMore": true }\n\n---\n\n9. RATE LIMITING:\n| Tier | Limit | Window | Headers Returned |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Unauthenticated | 60 req | Per hour | X-RateLimit-Limit, Remaining, Reset |\n| Authenticated user | 1000 req | Per hour | Same |\n| Premium / Enterprise | 10000 req | Per hour | Same |\n| Write endpoints (POST/PUT/DELETE) | 100 req | Per 15 min | Same |\n\nRate limit exceeded response: HTTP 429 with Retry-After header\n\n---\n\n10. VERSIONING AND DEPRECATION:\nBreaking change definition:\n  - Removing a field from response\n  - Changing a field type\n  - Removing or renaming an endpoint\n  - Changing authentication requirement\n\nDeprecation process:\n  Step 1: Add Deprecation header to affected endpoints: Deprecation: [date]\n  Step 2: Add Sunset header: Sunset: [date — minimum 6 months notice]\n  Step 3: Update API docs with migration guide\n  Step 4: Notify consumers via [e.g., email | changelog | developer portal]\n  Step 5: Remove endpoint on Sunset date\n\nNon-breaking changes (safe to make without version bump):\n  - Adding new optional fields to response\n  - Adding new optional query parameters\n  - Adding new endpoints
