ion, error messages, affected user reports, and any known context here]\n\nCONSTRAINTS:\n- Steps must be written so an L1 agent with no engineering background can follow them\n- Every step must be atomic — one action per step, never compound\n- Diagnostic steps must be platform-specific where iOS and Android differ\n- Resolution actions must be tied to a specific diagnosed cause — not generic fixes\n- Escalation criteria must be explicit conditions — not "if unsure, escalate"\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\nTROUBLESHOOTING GUIDE\nIssue Title: [Clear, searchable title — what fails + where + on what platform]\nGuide ID: TG-[NNN]\nPlatform: iOS | Android | Web | All\nSupport Tier: L1 | L2 | L3\nVersion: [X.X] | Last Updated: [DD/MM/YYYY]\n\n---\n\n1. ISSUE OVERVIEW:\nDescription: [Plain English — what the user experiences, not the technical cause]\nUser Impact: [e.g., Cannot log in | Data not saving | App crashes on launch]\nAffected Users: [e.g., All users | Users on iOS 17+ | Users with [specific config]]\nFrequency: Common | Intermittent | Rare | Unknown\n\n---\n\n2. SYMPTOM IDENTIFICATION:\nUse this guide if ALL of the following are true:\n  ✅ [Symptom 1 — e.g., "User reports error message: [exact message text]"]\n  ✅ [Symptom 2]\n  ✅ [Symptom 3]\n\nDo NOT use this guide if:\n  ❌ [Condition — e.g., "Error occurs only during checkout — use TG-[NNN] instead"]\n  ❌ [Condition]\n\n---\n\n3. PRE-INVESTIGATION CHECKLIST:\nCollect ALL of the following before starting diagnosis:\n  - [ ] App version number\n  - [ ] Device model and OS version\n  - [ ] Steps the user took before the issue occurred\n  - [ ] Error message text (exact — screenshot if possible)\n  - [ ] Time and frequency of occurrence\n  - [ ] Network type at time of issue (WiFi / Mobile data / VPN)\n  - [ ] [Additional item relevant to this issue]\n\n---\n\n4. DIAGNOSTIC STEPS:\nSTEP 1 — [Step title]\nAction: [Exact action to perform]\nPositive result (issue found): [What it means + go to Resolution A]\nNegative result (not this cause): [What it means + proceed to Step 2]\n\nSTEP 2 — [Step title]\nAction: [Exact action to perform]\nPositive result: [What it means + go to Resolution B]\nNegative result: [What it means + proceed to Step 3]\n\nSTEP 3 — [Step title]\nAction: [Exact action to perform]\nPositive result: [What it means + go to Resolution C]\nNegative result: [What it means + see Escalation Criteria]\n\n---\n(add steps as needed — order from least to most disruptive)\n\n---\n\n5. RESOLUTION ACTIONS:\nRESOLUTION A — [Root cause identified in Step 1]\nSteps:\n  1. [Action]\n  2. [Action]\n  3. [Action]\nExpected outcome: [What the user should see when resolved]\nVerification: [How to confirm the issue is resolved]\nIf unresolved after this: [Next action — or "Escalate per Section 6"]\n\nRESOLUTION B — [Root cause identified in Step 2]\nSteps:\n  1. [Action]\n  2. [Action]\nExpected outcome: [Expected outcome]\nVerification: [Verification step]\nIf unresolved after this: [Next action]\n\n---\n(repeat for every resolution)\n\n---\n\n6. ESCALATION CRITERIA:\nEscalate to [L2 / L3 / Engineering] immediately if ANY of the following are true:\n  🔴 [Condition — e.g., "Issue affects more than 10 users simultaneously"]\n  🔴 [Condition — e.g., "Data loss or corruption is reported"]\n  🔴 [Condition — e.g., "All diagnostic steps completed with no resolution found"]\n  🔴 [Condition — e.g., "Error code [X] appears in logs"]\n\nDo NOT escalate without completing Section 7 first.\n\n---\n\n7. ESCALATION PACKAGE:\nBefore escalating, collect and attach ALL of the following:\n  - [ ] Completed pre-investigation checklist (Section 3)\n  - [ ] Diagnostic steps completed and results of each\n  - [ ] Resolution actions attempted and outcomes\n  - [ ] Device logs / crash report / network trace (if accessible at this tier)\n  - [ ] Screenshots or screen recording of the issue\n  - [ ] Number of affected users and time of first report\n  - [ ] [Additional item specific to this issue]\n\nEscalation template:\n  Issue: [Guide ID] — [Issue Title]\n  Reported by: [User / Ticket ID]\n  Steps completed: [List]\n  Outcome: [What happened]\n  Attachments: [List]\n\n---\n\n8. PREVENTION:\n| Prevention Action | Who | Frequency | Outcome |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [e.g., Check app version on user login] | Support Agent | Each contact | Catch outdated app versions early |\n| [e.g., Monitor error rate dashboard] | L2 Support | Daily | Detect spikes before user volume escalates |\n| [e.g., Clear cache advisory in onboarding] | Product / L1 | One-time | Reduce cache-related tickets |\n\nKnown Recurrence Triggers:\n  - [e.g., "Issue recurs after app update — re-verify resolution after each release"]\n  - [e.g., "Issue more common on low-storage devices — advise storage check proactively"]\n\nRelated Guides:\n  | Guide ID | Title | When to Use Instead |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | TG-[NNN] | [Title] | [Condition] |
