ustomer tone, previous interactions, and any known context here]\n\nCONSTRAINTS:\n- Every template must open with the customer name field — never "Dear Customer"\n- Empathy statement must be genuine and specific to the issue — not copy-paste generic\n- Resolution template must explain what was fixed in plain English — no technical jargon\n- Known issue template must never over-promise a fix date — use ranges if uncertain\n- Closure template must include a satisfaction check — never just say "ticket closed"\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\nCUSTOMER RESPONSE TEMPLATES\nProduct: [Product Name] | Channel: [Channel] | Tone: [Tone]\nPrepared By: [Support Lead Name] | Date: [DD/MM/YYYY]\n\n---\n\nTEMPLATE 1 — INITIAL ACKNOWLEDGEMENT\nWhen to use: Send within SLA acknowledgement window upon receiving any new ticket\nSubject: Re: [Original subject line] — We've received your request [Ticket #]\n\nHi [Customer Name],\n\nThank you for reaching out to [Product Name] Support.\n\nI'm sorry to hear you're experiencing [brief plain-English description of their issue].\nI understand how frustrating this must be, especially [specific empathy statement relevant to issue impact].\n\nI've logged this as ticket [Ticket #] and I'm looking into it now. Here's what happens next:\n  - I'll investigate and aim to have an update for you by [Date/Time per SLA]\n  - If I need any additional information, I'll reach out directly to this thread\n  - You can track your ticket status at any time here: [Support portal link — or remove if not applicable]\n\nIf anything changes or the issue gets worse in the meantime, please don't hesitate to reply.\n\n[Your Name]\n[Product Name] Support Team\nTicket: [Ticket #] | Priority: [Standard/Priority/Enterprise]\n\n---\n\nTEMPLATE 2 — INVESTIGATION UPDATE\nWhen to use: Send when SLA update window is reached and issue is still under investigation\nSubject: Update on your request [Ticket #] — [Product Name] Support\n\nHi [Customer Name],\n\nI wanted to give you an update on ticket [Ticket #] regarding [brief issue description].\n\nI'm still actively investigating this and want to make sure I give you an accurate resolution\nrather than a quick answer that doesn't fully solve the problem.\n\nCurrent status: [One sentence on where the investigation stands — e.g., "I've reproduced the\nissue on our test environment and I'm working with the engineering team to identify the cause."]\n\nMy next update to you will be by [Date/Time].\n\nThank you for your patience — I appreciate it.\n\n[Your Name]\n[Product Name] Support Team\nTicket: [Ticket #]\n\n---\n\nTEMPLATE 3 — RESOLUTION RESPONSE\nWhen to use: Issue has been resolved — send confirmation and verify fix with customer\nSubject: Resolved: Your request [Ticket #] — [Product Name] Support\n\nHi [Customer Name],\n\nGreat news — I've resolved the issue you reported regarding [brief issue description].\n\nHere's what was happening and what I've done to fix it:\n[Plain English explanation of root cause — no jargon]\n[Plain English explanation of fix applied]\n\nTo confirm the fix is working on your end, please:\n  1. [Verification step 1 — e.g., "Open the app and attempt to log in"]\n  2. [Verification step 2]\n\nIf everything looks good, no action is needed — I'll close this ticket in 48 hours.\nIf you're still experiencing any issues, please reply to this email and I'll pick it up immediately.\n\n[Your Name]\n[Product Name] Support Team\nTicket: [Ticket #]\n\n---\n\nTEMPLATE 4 — ESCALATION NOTICE\nWhen to use: Issue requires escalation to L2/L3 or engineering — inform customer without alarm\nSubject: Update on your request [Ticket #] — [Product Name] Support\n\nHi [Customer Name],\n\nThank you for your patience while I've been investigating ticket [Ticket #].\n\nTo make sure your issue gets the fastest and most accurate resolution, I've escalated this\nto our specialist [L2/L3/Engineering] team who have deeper technical expertise in this area.\nThis is a standard part of our process for issues of this type — not an indication that\nanything is seriously wrong.\n\nWhat this means for you:\n  - Your ticket remains open and active — nothing is being dropped\n  - The specialist team will pick this up by [Date/Time]\n  - I'll remain your point of contact — all updates will come through this thread\n\nThank you for bearing with us.\n\n[Your Name]\n[Product Name] Support Team\nTicket: [Ticket #]\n\n---\n\nTEMPLATE 5 — KNOWN ISSUE UPDATE\n⚠️ Review tone carefully — do not over-promise resolution timeline\nWhen to use: Customer has reported an issue that matches a known platform defect\nSubject: Known issue update for your request [Ticket #] — [Product Name] Support\n\nHi [Customer Name],\n\nThank you for reporting this — I want to be transparent with you.\n\nThe issue you're experiencing with [brief issue description] is a known issue that our\nengineering team is actively working to resolve. You are not alone in experiencing this,\nand I'm sorry for the disruption it's causing.\n\nCurrent status: [One sentence on engineering progress — e.g., "A fix has been identified\nand is currently being tested."]\nExpected resolution: [Honest range — e.g., "We expect to release a fix within the next\n3–5 business days, though this may change as testing progresses."]\n\nIn the meantime, [workaround if available — or remove this sentence if no workaround exists].\n\nI'll update you as soon as the fix is released. You don't need to do anything — I'll be\nin touch directly.\n\n[Your Name]\n[Product Name] Support Team\nTicket: [Ticket #]\n\n---\n\nTEMPLATE 6 — NO FAULT FOUND RESPONSE\nWhen to use: Investigation completed with no reproducible issue or platform defect found\nSubject: Update on your request [Ticket #] — [Product Name] Support\n\nHi [Customer Name],\n\nThank you for your patience while I investigated ticket [Ticket #].\n\nAfter a thorough investigation, I wasn't able to reproduce the issue on our end and our\nsystems are showing [product/feature] working as expected.