 complete a section is missing, flag as [NEEDS DATA] — never fabricate.\n\nINCIDENT DATA AND INVESTIGATION FINDINGS:\n[Paste incident reports, logs, error messages, monitoring alerts, timeline data,\nand any investigation notes here]\n\nCONSTRAINTS:\n- Root cause must be supported by evidence — not assumption\n- Timeline must use actual timestamps — not relative terms like "shortly after"\n- Impact must be quantified where possible — number of users, duration, data affected\n- Corrective and preventive actions must be distinct — corrective fixes this incident,\n  preventive stops the next one\n- Blame language is strictly prohibited — findings must be system and process focused\n- Document must be suitable for the audience stated in CONTEXT — adjust technical depth accordingly\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\nROOT CAUSE ANALYSIS SUMMARY\nProduct: [Product Name] | Incident ID: [ID] | Severity: [P1/P2/P3/P4]\nPlatform: [iOS/Android/Web/All] | Environment: [Production/Staging]\nIncident Date: [DD/MM/YYYY] | Resolution Date: [DD/MM/YYYY]\nPrepared By: [Name] | Report Date: [DD/MM/YYYY] | Status: Draft | Final\n\n---\n\n1. INCIDENT SUMMARY:\nWhat happened: [2-3 sentences — plain English, no jargon]\nFirst detected: [DD/MM/YYYY HH:MM]\nFully resolved: [DD/MM/YYYY HH:MM]\nTotal duration: [X hours Y minutes]\nUsers affected: [N users — or "Unknown — NEEDS DATA"]\nBusiness impact: [e.g., "Checkout unavailable for 2.5 hours — estimated [N] failed transactions"]\n\n---\n\n2. INCIDENT TIMELINE:\n| Time (UTC) | Event | Detected By | Action Taken |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [HH:MM] | [Event — e.g., "Spike in error rate detected"] | [e.g., Monitoring alert] | [e.g., On-call engineer paged] |\n| [HH:MM] | [Event] | [Detected by] | [Action] |\n| [HH:MM] | [Event] | [Detected by] | [Action] |\n| [HH:MM] | [e.g., "Service fully restored"] | [Detected by] | [e.g., Incident closed"] |\n\nDetection Gap: Time between incident start and first detection: [X minutes]\nResponse Gap: Time between detection and first action: [X minutes]\n\n---\n\n3. ROOT CAUSE IDENTIFICATION (5-Why Analysis):\nProblem Statement: [One sentence — what failed]\n\nWhy 1: [First level cause]\nWhy 2: [Deeper cause]\nWhy 3: [Deeper still]\nWhy 4: [Deeper still]\nWhy 5 (Root Cause): [The true underlying system or process failure]\n\nRoot Cause Statement:\n[One clear sentence summarising the root cause — system/process focused, no blame]\n\nEvidence Supporting Root Cause:\n  - [Evidence 1 — e.g., "Error logs show [X] at [timestamp]"]\n  - [Evidence 2]\n  - [Evidence 3]\n\n---\n\n4. CONTRIBUTING FACTORS:\n| Factor | Description | Why It Matters |\n|---|---|---|\n| [e.g., Missing monitoring alert] | [Alert threshold not configured for this error type] | [Delayed detection by X minutes] |\n| [e.g., No automated rollback] | [Deployment pipeline lacked rollback trigger] | [Extended resolution time] |\n| [Additional factor] | [Description] | [Impact] |\n\n---\n\n5. IMPACT ASSESSMENT:\nTechnical Impact:\n  | Component | Impact | Duration |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | [e.g., Login service] | [e.g., 100% failure rate] | [e.g., 2h 30m] |\n  | [e.g., Database] | [e.g., Read-only mode] | [e.g., 1h 45m] |\n\nBusiness Impact:\n  | Metric | Value |\n  |---|---|\n  | Users affected | [N — or NEEDS DATA] |\n  | Failed transactions / sessions | [N — or NEEDS DATA] |\n  | Estimated revenue impact | [Value — or "Not quantified"] |\n  | SLA breached | Yes — [SLA details] | No |\n  | Client notifications required | Yes | No |\n\nSeverity Justification: [Why this was rated P1/P2/P3/P4]\n\n---\n\n6. RESOLUTION ACTIONS (immediate — what stopped the incident):\n| Action | Who | Time Taken | Outcome |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [e.g., Rolled back deployment to v[X]] | [Role] | [HH:MM] | [e.g., Error rate returned to normal] |\n| [e.g., Restarted affected service] | [Role] | [HH:MM] | [Outcome] |\n| [e.g., Cleared corrupted cache] | [Role] | [HH:MM] | [Outcome] |\n\nTime to Resolve: [Total duration from first action to full resolution]\n\n---\n\n7. CORRECTIVE ACTIONS (permanent fix for this specific root cause):\n| # | Action | Owner | Priority | Due Date | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | [Specific fix — e.g., "Add input validation to [endpoint] to reject [condition]"] | [Role] | High | [DD/MM/YYYY] | Open |\n| 2 | [Specific fix] | [Role] | High | [DD/MM/YYYY] | Open |\n\n---\n\n8. PREVENTIVE ACTIONS (systemic changes to stop recurrence):\n| # | Action | Owner | Priority | Due Date | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | [Systemic change — e.g., "Add automated alert for error rate >5% on all critical endpoints"] | [Role] | High | [DD/MM/YYYY] | Open |\n| 2 | [e.g., "Add rollback trigger to deployment pipeline for P1 error rate threshold"] | [Role] | High | [DD/MM/YYYY] | Open |\n| 3 | [e.g., "Add this scenario to regression suite to catch regression in future releases"] | [Role] | Medium | [DD/MM/YYYY] | Open |\n\n---\n\n9. LESSONS LEARNED:\n| # | Lesson | Apply To | Owner |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | [What the team now knows — e.g., "Monitoring was not configured for this error class"] | [e.g., All new service deployments] | [Role] |\n| 2 | [Lesson] | [Apply to] | [Role] |\n| 3 | [Lesson] | [Apply to] | [Role] |\n\nWhat went well:\n  - [e.g., "On-call response was fast once alert was received"]\n  - [e.g., "Rollback procedure was well documented and executed correctly"]\n\nWhat could have gone better:\n  - [e.g., "Detection took X minutes longer than it should have"]\n  - [e.g., "Client communication was delayed — no template was available"]\n\n---\n\n10. ACTION REGISTER:\n| # | Action | Type | Owner | Priority | Due Date | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | [Action] | Corrective | [Role] | High | [DD/MM/YYYY] | Open |\n| 2 | [Action] | Corrective | [Role] | High | [DD/MM/YYYY] | Open |\n| 3 | [Action] | Preventive | [Role] | High | [DD/MM/YYYY] | Open |\n| 4 | [Action] | Preventive | [Role] | Medium | [DD/MM/YYYY] | Open |\n\n---\n\nREPORT APPROVAL:\n| Role | Name | Status | Date |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| L3 Support Lead | [Name] | Approved / Pending | [DD/MM/YYYY] |\n| Engineering Manager | [Name] | Approved / Pending | [DD/MM/YYYY] |\n| Product Manager | [Name] | Approved / Pending | [DD/MM/YYYY] |
