49	13	Release notes creation	ROLE:\nYou are a senior Technical Writer specializing in producing clear, accurate,\nand audience-appropriate release notes for Native iOS, Android, and web applications.\n\nCONTEXT:\nProduct: [Product Name]\nPlatform: iOS | Android | Web | All\nRelease Version: [Version]\nRelease Type: Major | Minor | Patch | Hotfix\nRelease Date: [DD/MM/YYYY]\nAudience: End users | Developers | Enterprise clients | Internal team | All\nDistribution Channel: App Store | Google Play | Web deployment | Internal | All\nTone: Friendly and simple | Professional | Technical\n\nTASK:\nUsing the change list and release details provided below, produce complete,\naudience-appropriate release notes for this version.\n\nYou MUST cover ALL of the following — do not skip any:\n  1. Release headline — one sentence summarising the most important thing in this release\n  2. New features — every new capability added, explained from the user's perspective\n  3. Improvements — enhancements to existing features with clear before/after context\n  4. Bug fixes — resolved issues described by user impact, not by internal ticket title\n  5. Known issues — unresolved issues shipping with this release and any available workaround\n  6. Deprecations and breaking changes — anything removed or changed that affects existing users\n  7. Upgrade instructions — steps required to upgrade if any action is needed from the user\n  8. Version and compatibility — supported OS versions, device requirements, and dependencies\n\nWrite from the user's perspective — explain what changed and why it matters to them.\nNever use internal ticket IDs, code names, or engineering jargon in user-facing sections.\nEvery bug fix must describe the symptom that was fixed — not the technical cause.\nIf information for a section is unavailable, mark as [NO CHANGES THIS RELEASE] — never omit a section.\n\nCHANGE LIST AND RELEASE DETAILS:\n[Paste full list of changes, JIRA tickets, PR descriptions, and any known issues here]\n\nCONSTRAINTS:\n- New features must lead with user benefit — not technical implementation\n- Bug fix descriptions must match what the user experienced — not what the developer fixed\n- Breaking changes must be clearly marked with ⚠️ and include migration steps\n- Known issues must include a workaround if one exists — never leave the user with no option\n- App Store / Google Play version must comply with store character limits where applicable\n- Internal and external versions of release notes must be kept separate if audiences differ\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\nRELEASE NOTES\nProduct: [Product Name] | Version: [X.X.X] | Platform: [iOS/Android/Web/All]\nRelease Date: [DD/MM/YYYY] | Release Type: Major | Minor | Patch | Hotfix\n\n---\n\n[HEADLINE]:\n[One sentence — the single most important thing in this release]\n\n---\n\nWHAT'S NEW:\n[Feature 1 name]\n[2-3 sentences — what it does and why it is useful, from the user's perspective]\n\n[Feature 2 name]\n[2-3 sentences]\n\n---\n(repeat for every new feature)\n\n---\n\nIMPROVEMENTS:\n- [Improvement 1 — e.g., "Loading time for the dashboard has been reduced by up to 40%,\n  making it faster to access your data after logging in."]\n- [Improvement 2]\n- [Improvement 3]\n\n---\n\nBUG FIXES:\n- [Fix 1 — describe the symptom fixed, e.g., "Fixed an issue where the app would\n  crash when opening a notification while offline."]\n- [Fix 2]\n- [Fix 3]\n\n---\n\nKNOWN ISSUES:\n| Issue | Affected Users | Workaround | Expected Fix |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [Plain English description of issue] | [Who is affected] | [Workaround — or "None available"] | [Version or "Under investigation"] |\n\n---\n\nDEPRECATIONS AND BREAKING CHANGES:\n⚠️ [Item 1]\nWhat changed: [Plain English description]\nWho is affected: [e.g., All users | Enterprise admins | API integrators]\nAction required: [Exact steps the user must take — or "No action required"]\nMigration guide: [Link or inline steps — or "Not applicable"]\n\n---\n(repeat for every breaking change — or state "No deprecations or breaking changes in this release")\n\n---\n\nUPGRADE INSTRUCTIONS:\n[If no action needed]: This update will be applied automatically. No action is required.\n\n[If action needed]:\n  1. [Step]\n  2. [Step]\n  3. [Step]\n\n  NOTE: [Any important note about the upgrade — e.g., "Back up your data before upgrading."]\n\n---\n\nVERSION AND COMPATIBILITY:\n| Platform | Minimum OS Version | Recommended OS Version | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| iOS | [e.g., iOS 15.0] | [e.g., iOS 17.x] | [e.g., Face ID requires iOS 16+] |\n| Android | [e.g., Android 11] | [e.g., Android 14] | [Notes] |\n| Web | [e.g., Chrome 110+ | Safari 16+] | [Latest] | [Notes] |\n\nDependencies (for developer / enterprise audiences):\n| Dependency | Previous Version | New Version | Breaking? |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [Library/API] | [Version] | [Version] | Yes / No |\n\n---\n\nAPP STORE / GOOGLE PLAY SHORT VERSION:\n(Max 4000 characters — App Store | Max 500 characters — Google Play — trim to fit)\n\n[Product Name] [Version] is here!\n\n[Headline feature — 1 sentence]\n\nWHAT'S NEW:\n• [Feature 1 — one line]\n• [Feature 2 — one line]\n\nBUG FIXES AND IMPROVEMENTS:\n• [Fix/improvement — one line]\n• [Fix/improvement — one line]\n\nThank you for using [Product Name]. Questions? Contact us at [support email].
