 DETAIL] — never fabricate.\n\nPROCESS DESCRIPTION AND STEPS:\n[Paste process description, existing notes, runbook content, or verbal walkthrough here]\n\nCONSTRAINTS:\n- Steps must be written so the stated audience can follow without prior knowledge of this process\n- Every step must have a clear completion indicator — how does the person know the step is done?\n- Decision points must cover ALL possible outcomes — no unhandled branches\n- Error handling must specify: what went wrong, immediate action, and escalation path\n- SOP must be version-controlled — every change must increment the version number\n- Compliance-sensitive processes must include audit trail requirements where applicable\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\nSTANDARD OPERATING PROCEDURE\nSOP ID: SOP-[NNN]\nTitle: [Process Name]\nCategory: [Category stated in CONTEXT]\nVersion: [X.X] | Status: Draft | Approved | Under Review\nEffective Date: [DD/MM/YYYY] | Review Date: [DD/MM/YYYY]\nOwner: [Role — e.g., QA Lead | DevOps Engineer | Support Manager]\nApproved By: [Role]\n\n---\n\n1. PURPOSE:\n[2-3 sentences — why this process exists, what problem it solves, and what happens if it is not followed]\n\n---\n\n2. SCOPE:\nApplies to: [Who must follow this SOP]\nCovers: [What this SOP includes]\nDoes NOT cover: [What is explicitly out of scope — and which SOP covers it instead]\n\n---\n\n3. ROLES AND RESPONSIBILITIES:\n| Role | Responsibility in This Process |\n|---|---|\n| [Role 1] | [What they do — e.g., "Initiates the process and completes Steps 1–4"] |\n| [Role 2] | [What they do — e.g., "Reviews and approves at Step 7"] |\n| [Role 3] | [What they do] |\n\nRACI Summary:\n| Step | Responsible | Accountable | Consulted | Informed |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [Step group or phase] | [Role] | [Role] | [Role] | [Role] |\n\n---\n\n4. PREREQUISITES:\nBefore starting this procedure, confirm ALL of the following:\n  - [ ] [Prerequisite 1 — e.g., "You have [system] access with [permission level]"]\n  - [ ] [Prerequisite 2 — e.g., "The [environment] is in a stable state"]\n  - [ ] [Prerequisite 3 — e.g., "The change has been approved by [Role]"]\n  - [ ] [Prerequisite 4]\n\nTools and access required:\n  | Tool / System | Access Level Required | How to Request if Missing |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | [Tool] | [e.g., Admin | Read-only | Write] | [e.g., Submit access request to IT via [link]] |\n\n---\n\n5. PROCEDURE STEPS:\n\nPHASE [N] — [Phase name, e.g., "Preparation"]:\n\nSTEP [N.N] — [Step title]\nAction: [Exactly what to do — one action only]\nHow to do it: [Detailed instruction if needed — or "Self-explanatory"]\nCompletion indicator: [How you know this step is done — e.g., "System shows confirmation message: [text]"]\nEstimated time: [e.g., 2 minutes | <1 minute]\nScreenshot / reference: [SCREENSHOT: description — or link to reference — or "None"]\n\nSTEP [N.N] — [Step title]\nAction: [Action]\nHow to do it: [Instruction]\nCompletion indicator: [Indicator]\nEstimated time: [Time]\n\n---\n(repeat steps within each phase)\n\n---\n\nPHASE [N+1] — [Next phase name]:\n(repeat step format)\n\n---\n\n6. DECISION POINTS:\n\nDECISION [N] — [Decision title] (occurs after Step [N.N]):\nCondition: [What you are evaluating]\n\nIF [Condition A — e.g., "Build passes all checks"]:\n  → THEN proceed to Step [N.N]\n\nIF [Condition B — e.g., "Build fails one or more checks"]:\n  → THEN go to Error Handling — Scenario [N]\n\nIF [Condition C — e.g., "Uncertain / cannot determine"]:\n  → THEN stop and escalate to [Role] before proceeding\n\n---\n(repeat for every decision point in the process)\n\n---\n\n7. ERROR HANDLING:\n\nSCENARIO [N] — [Error scenario title]\nTrigger: [What causes this scenario — e.g., "Step 3.2 returns error code [X]"]\nImmediate action:\n  1. [Stop / do not proceed action]\n  2. [Diagnostic or containment action]\n  3. [Recovery action if known]\nEscalation path:\n  - If resolved by Step [N]: continue from Step [N]\n  - If NOT resolved within [N minutes]: escalate to [Role] via [channel — e.g., Slack #ops-escalation]\n  - If data loss or security risk detected: escalate to [Role] IMMEDIATELY — do not attempt further steps\nDocumentation required: [What must be logged — e.g., error message, timestamp, steps taken]\n\n---\n(repeat for every error scenario)\n\n---\n\n8. VERIFICATION AND SIGN-OFF:\n\nPost-completion checklist:\n  - [ ] [Verification item 1 — e.g., "Confirm deployment is live at [URL]"]\n  - [ ] [Verification item 2 — e.g., "Smoke test passes — use SOP-[NNN]"]\n  - [ ] [Verification item 3 — e.g., "Monitoring shows no error rate spike"]\n  - [ ] [Verification item 4 — e.g., "Completion logged in [system]"]\n\nSign-off required:\n| Role | Name | Signature / Approval | Date |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [Role 1] | [Name] | Approved / Not Approved | [DD/MM/YYYY] |\n| [Role 2] | [Name] | Approved / Not Approved | [DD/MM/YYYY] |\n\nAudit trail: [Where completion is recorded — e.g., JIRA ticket | Confluence log | Email confirmation]\n\n---\n\n9. RELATED DOCUMENTS:\n| Document | Type | When to Use |\n|---|---|---|\n| [SOP-NNN — Title] | SOP | [When this related SOP applies] |\n| [Runbook title] | Runbook | [When to use] |\n| [Policy title] | Policy | [Reference for compliance] |\n\n---\n\n10. VERSION HISTORY:\n| Version | Date | Author | Changes Made | Approved By |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1.0 | [DD/MM/YYYY] | [Name] | Initial version | [Name] |\n| [X.X] | [DD/MM/YYYY] | [Name] | [What changed] | [Name] |
