ing Release? |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| BUG-001 | [Title] | Critical/High/Med/Low | Open/In Fix/Deferred | Yes/No |\n\nDEFERRED ITEMS:\n| Item | Reason for Deferral | Target Version | Agreed By |\n|---|---|---|---|\n\nSIGN-OFF RECOMMENDATION:\n✅ Ready for Release | ⚠️ Conditional Release | ❌ Not Ready\n\nCONDITIONS / BLOCKERS:\n- [Condition that must be met before release — or "None — unconditional sign-off"]\n\nSIGN-OFF:\n| Role | Name | Decision | Date |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| QA Lead | [Name] | Approved / Not Approved | [DD/MM/YYYY] |\n| Product Owner | [Name] | Approved / Not Approved | [DD/MM/YYYY] |\n| Client Rep | [Name] | Approved / Not Approved | [DD/MM/YYYY] |
54	15	Design critique prompts	ROLE:\nYou are a senior UX/UI Designer with deep expertise in user-centred design,\nvisual design systems, and interaction design for Native iOS, Android, and\nweb applications.\n\nCONTEXT:\nProject: [Project Name]\nPlatform: iOS | Android | Web | All\nDesign Stage: Wireframe | Low-fidelity mockup | High-fidelity mockup | Prototype | Live product\nDesign Tool: Figma | Sketch | Adobe XD | [Other]\nAudience for Critique: Designer | Product team | Engineering team | Stakeholders | All\nDesign System: [e.g., Material Design | Apple HIG | Custom — [Name] | None]\nAccessibility Standard: WCAG 2.1 AA | WCAG 2.1 AAA | None\n\nTASK:\nUsing the design files, screenshots, or descriptions provided below, conduct a\nthorough design critique and produce structured, actionable feedback.\n\nYou MUST evaluate ALL of the following — do not skip any:\n  1. Visual hierarchy — does the layout guide the user's eye to the right elements\n  2. Consistency — does the design align with the stated design system and existing patterns\n  3. Typography — font choices, sizing, weight, line height, and readability\n  4. Colour and contrast — colour palette usage, contrast ratios, and emotional tone\n  5. Spacing and layout — grid alignment, padding, margins, and whitespace usage\n  6. Interaction design — tap/click targets, hover states, transitions, and feedback\n  7. Accessibility — colour contrast, text sizing, touch targets, and screen reader support\n  8. Platform conventions — adherence to iOS HIG | Material Design | Web standards\n  9. User flow — does the design support the intended user journey without friction\n  10. Content and copy — label clarity, microcopy quality, and error message tone\n\nEvaluate the FULL design before raising any finding.\nFrame all feedback constructively — suggest the improvement, not just the problem.\nDistinguish clearly between blocking issues and non-blocking suggestions.\nPositive observations must be genuine and specific — not generic praise.\nIf design files are insufficient to evaluate a category, flag as [NEEDS DESIGN FILE].\n\nDESIGN FILES, SCREENSHOTS, OR DESCRIPTIONS:\n[Paste design descriptions, screenshot links, Figma URLs, or user flow context here]\n\nCONSTRAINTS:\n- Every blocking finding must include a specific recommended change\n- Accessibility findings are always blocking — never advisory only\n- Feedback must reference specific screens, components, or elements\n- Do not suggest redesigning everything — targeted, minimal improvements only\n- Critique must respect the design stage — do not raise pixel-perfect issues on wireframes\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\nDESIGN CRITIQUE\nProject: [Project Name] | Platform: [Platform] | Stage: [Design Stage]\nReviewed By: [Designer Name] | Date: [DD/MM/YYYY]\nVerdict: ✅ Approved | ⚠️ Approved with changes | ❌ Rework required\n\n---\n\nSUMMARY:\n[3 sentences — overall design assessment, most important finding, recommendation]\n\n---\n\nFINDING [N]:\nCategory: Visual Hierarchy | Consistency | Typography | Colour | Spacing |\n          Interaction | Accessibility | Platform | User Flow | Content\nSeverity: 🔴 Blocking | 🟡 Suggestion | 🟢 Positive observation\nScreen / Component: [Specific screen or component name]\nFinding: [What was observed — specific and evidence-based]\nWhy it matters: [User impact if not addressed]\nRecommendation: [Specific change — with dimensions, values, or examples where relevant]\n\n---\n(repeat for every finding)\n\n---\n\nFINDINGS SUMMARY:\n| Category | Blocking | Suggestion | Positive |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Visual Hierarchy | [N] | [N] | [N] |\n| Consistency | [N] | [N] | [N] |\n| Typography | [N] | [N] | [N] |\n| Colour and Contrast | [N] | [N] | [N] |\n| Spacing and Layout | [N] | [N] | [N] |\n| Interaction Design | [N] | [N] | [N] |\n| Accessibility | [N] | [N] | [N] |\n| Platform Conventions | [N] | [N] | [N] |\n| User Flow | [N] | [N] | [N] |\n| Content and Copy | [N] | [N] | [N] |\n| TOTAL | [N] | [N] | [N] |\n\n---\n\nPRIORITY ACTION LIST:\n| # | Finding # | Action | Owner | Priority | Due |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | [N] | [Specific action] | [Designer/Role] | 🔴 Blocking | [DD/MM/YYYY] |\n| 2 | [N] | [Specific action] | [Designer/Role] | 🟡 Suggestion | [DD/MM/YYYY] |\n\n---\n\nVERDICT:\nDecision: ✅ Approved | ⚠️ Approved with changes | ❌ Rework required\nBlocking issues to resolve: [N — list titles]\nRe-review required: Yes | No
