ainful step: Step [N] — [Evidence]\n\n---\n\n3. HEURISTIC EVALUATION:\n(Nielsen's 10 Usability Heuristics)\n\n| # | Heuristic | Rating | Finding | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Visibility of system status | 🔴/🟡/🟢 | [Finding] | [Evidence] |\n| 2 | Match between system and real world | 🔴/🟡/🟢 | [Finding] | [Evidence] |\n| 3 | User control and freedom | 🔴/🟡/🟢 | [Finding] | [Evidence] |\n| 4 | Consistency and standards | 🔴/🟡/🟢 | [Finding] | [Evidence] |\n| 5 | Error prevention | 🔴/🟡/🟢 | [Finding] | [Evidence] |\n| 6 | Recognition over recall | 🔴/🟡/🟢 | [Finding] | [Evidence] |\n| 7 | Flexibility and efficiency of use | 🔴/🟡/🟢 | [Finding] | [Evidence] |\n| 8 | Aesthetic and minimalist design | 🔴/🟡/🟢 | [Finding] | [Evidence] |\n| 9 | Help users recognise and recover from errors | 🔴/🟡/🟢 | [Finding] | [Evidence] |\n| 10 | Help and documentation | 🔴/🟡/🟢 | [Finding] | [Evidence] |\n\nRating: 🔴 Fails heuristic | 🟡 Partially meets | 🟢 Meets heuristic\n\n---\n\n4. FRICTION POINT ANALYSIS:\nFRICTION POINT [N]:\nScreen / Flow: [Specific screen or flow]\nWhat happens: [What the user experiences]\nEvidence: [Data supporting this — e.g., "62% drop-off on this screen per analytics"]\nUser impact: High | Medium | Low\nBusiness impact: High | Medium | Low\nRoot cause: [Why this friction exists — design, copy, technical, or flow issue]\nRecommendation: [Specific fix]\n\n---\n(repeat for every friction point)\n\n---\n\n5. ACCESSIBILITY AUDIT:\n| WCAG Criterion | Level | Status | Issue | Affected Users | Fix |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1.1.1 Non-text content | A | ✅/❌ | [Issue — or "Pass"] | [Who] | [Fix] |\n| 1.4.3 Contrast minimum | AA | ✅/❌ | [e.g., "Button text #777 on #FFF = 4.1:1 — fails AA"] | Low vision | [Fix] |\n| 1.4.4 Resize text | AA | ✅/❌ | [Issue] | [Who] | [Fix] |\n| 2.1.1 Keyboard | A | ✅/❌ | [Issue] | Keyboard users | [Fix] |\n| 2.4.3 Focus order | A | ✅/❌ | [Issue] | Screen reader users | [Fix] |\n| 3.3.1 Error identification | A | ✅/❌ | [Issue] | [Who] | [Fi