n, PII handling, access control, and audit logging\n\nEvaluate the FULL pipeline requirements before designing any component.\nEvery design decision must include the reason it was chosen over alternatives.\nIf requirements are ambiguous or missing, flag as [NEEDS CLARIFICATION] — never assume.\n\nPIPELINE REQUIREMENTS AND DATA CONTEXT:\n[Paste source system details, target schema, transformation rules, volume estimates,\nfrequency requirements, and any existing pipeline context here]\n\nCONSTRAINTS:\n- Pipeline must be idempotent — safe to rerun at any step without side effects\n- All PII fields must be identified and handled per compliance requirements\n- Error handling must be explicit — silent failures are not acceptable\n- Performance estimates must reference actual data volumes provided\n- Code examples must be complete and runnable — no placeholder logic\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\nETL PIPELINE DESIGN\nProject: [Project Name] | Type: [Pipeline Type]\nSource: [Source Systems] -> Target: [Target Systems]\nPrepared By: [Engineer Name] | Date: [DD/MM/YYYY]\n\n---\n\n1. PIPELINE ARCHITECTURE:\nOverview: [2-3 sentences describing the end-to-end pipeline]\n\nComponents:\n| Component | Tool / Technology | Purpose | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Extraction | [Tool] | [Purpose] | [Notes] |\n| Staging | [Tool] | [Purpose] | [Notes] |\n| Transformation | [Tool] | [Purpose] | [Notes] |\n| Loading | [Tool] | [Purpose] | [Notes] |\n| Orchestration | [Tool] | [Purpose] | [Notes] |\n| Monitoring | [Tool] | [Purpose] | [Notes] |\n| Error handling | [Tool] | [Purpose] | [Notes] |\n\nDesign decision: [Key architectural choice and why it was made over alternatives]\n\n---\n\n2. EXTRACTION LOGIC:\nStrategy: Full load | Incremental | CDC | Hybrid\nIncremental key: [e.g., updated_at timestamp | sequence ID | CDC log offset]\n\nWatermark management:\n  - Storage: [e.g., metadata table | Airflow XCom | S3 state file]\n  - Update strategy: [e.g., Update watermark only after successful load]\n  - Failure handling: [e.g., On failure, retain previous watermark for safe rerun]\n\n---\n\n3. TRANSFORMATION LOGIC:\nTransformations applied:\n| Step | Transformation | Input | Output | Business Rule |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | [e.g., Type casting] | [Input field] | [Output field] | [Rule] |\n| 2 | [e.g., Null handling] | [Input field] | [Output field] | [Rule] |\n| 3 | [e.g., Enrichment join] | [Input field] | [Output field] | [Rule] |\n| 4 | [e.g., Deduplication] | [Input field] | [Output field] | [Rule] |\n\nPII fields identified:\n| Field | PII Type | Handling | Compliance Requirement |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [Field name] | [e.g., Email | Phone | ID] | [e.g., Hash | Mask | Encrypt | Tokenise] | [e.g., GDPR | PDPA | Other] |\n\n---\n\n4. LOADING STRATEGY:\nStrategy: Append | Upsert (MERGE) | Overwrite | SCD Type 1 | SCD Type 2\nTarget table: [Schema].[Table name]\nPrimary / merge key: [Key field(s)]\nPartitioning: [e.g., Partition by date column | No partitioning]\nEstimated load time: [e.g., ~12 mins for 50M rows at current volume]\n\n---\n\n5. ERROR HANDLING:\n| Error Type | Detection Method | Action | Retry | Alert |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Source connection failure | Connection timeout | Retry with backoff | 3x — 5 min intervals | PagerDuty / Slack |\n| Schema mismatch | Schema validation check | Route to dead letter | No retry | Email + Slack |\n| Transformation failure | Row-level try/except | Log + dead letter queue | No retry | Slack alert |\n| Load failure | DB exception catch | Rollback + alert | 2x retry | PagerDuty |\n| Data quality failure | DQ check post-load | Quarantine table | No retry | Slack alert |\n\nDead letter queue:\n  - Storage: [e.g., S3 bucket | PostgreSQL quarantine table | Kafka DLQ topic]\n  - Schema: [e.g., original_payload | error_message | pipeline_run_id | failed_at]\n  - Review process: [e.g., Daily review by on-call engineer — reprocess or discard]\n\n---\n\n6. DATA QUALITY CHECKS:\n| Check | Type | Field(s) | Rule | Action