ry design decision must include the reason it was chosen over alternatives.\nIf requirements are ambiguous or missing, flag as [NEEDS CLARIFICATION] — never assume.\nDDL must be complete and runnable — not pseudocode or partial definitions.\n\nDATA REQUIREMENTS AND SYSTEM CONTEXT:\n[Paste entity descriptions, relationships, query patterns, volume estimates,\naccess patterns, and any existing schema context here]\n\nCONSTRAINTS:\n- All tables must have explicit primary keys — no implicit row identifiers\n- All foreign keys must be explicitly defined with ON DELETE behaviour\n- Every data type choice must be justified — no lazy VARCHAR(255) everywhere\n- PII fields must be identified and flagged in every table they appear\n- Schema must support the stated query patterns without full table scans\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\nSCHEMA DESIGN\nProject: [Project Name] | Database: [Database Type]\nUse Case: [Use Case] | Model: [Data Model]\nPrepared By: [Engineer Name] | Date: [DD/MM/YYYY]\n\n---\n\n1. SCHEMA OVERVIEW:\nPurpose: [What this schema stores and serves]\nDesign pattern chosen: [e.g., 3NF relational | Star schema | Wide table | Hybrid]\nWhy this pattern: [Reason this pattern fits the use case over alternatives]\nKey design decisions:\n  - [Decision 1 and rationale]\n  - [Decision 2 and rationale]\n  - [Decision 3 and rationale]\n\n---\n\n2. ENTITY RELATIONSHIP DESIGN:\nEntities:\n| Entity | Description | Estimated Rows | Growth Rate |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [Entity name] | [What it represents] | [e.g., 10M] | [e.g., +500K/month] |\n\nRelationships:\n| Entity A | Relationship | Entity B | Cardinality | FK Direction |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [Entity] | [e.g., places] | [Entity] | One-to-many | [Entity A] -> [Entity B] |\n| [Entity] | [e.g., belongs to] | [Entity] | Many-to-one | [Entity B] -> [Entity A] |\n\nER Diagram (text):\n[Entity A] ---< [Entity B] >--- [Entity C]\n     |                               |\n  [Entity D]                   [Entity E]\n\n---\n\n3. TABLE DEFINITIONS:\n-- [Table name]: [Purpose]\nCREATE TABLE [schema].[table_name] (\n    [column_name]     [DATA TYPE]        [CONSTRAINTS],\n    [column_name]     [DATA TYPE]        [CONSTRAINTS],\n    -- PII: [field] — [PII type] — [handling]\n    created_at        TIMESTAMPTZ        NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),\n    updated_at        TIMESTAMPTZ        NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),\n    CONSTRAINT [pk_name] PRIMARY KEY ([column]),\n    CONSTRAINT [fk_name] FOREIGN KEY ([column])\n        REFERENCES [schema].[ref_table] ([column])\n        ON DELETE [RESTRICT | CASCADE | SET NULL],\n    CONSTRAINT [uq_name] UNIQUE ([column]),\n    CONSTRAINT [ck_name] CHECK ([condition])\n);\n\n(repeat complete DDL for every table)\n\n---\n\n4. INDEXING STRATEGY:\n| Table | Index Name | Type | Columns | Purpose | Estimated Benefit |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [Table] | [idx_name] | B-tree | [column(s)] | [e.g., PK lookup] | [e.g., O(log n) lookup] |\n| [Table] | [idx_name] | B-tree | [col1, col2] | [e.g., Composite filter] | [e.g., Avoids seq scan] |\n| [Table] | [idx_name] | Hash | [column] | [e.g., Equality lookup] | [e.g., O(1) lookup] |\n| [Table] | [idx_name] | GIN | [column] | [e.g., JSONB / full-text search] | [e.g., Fast text search] |\n| [Table] | [idx_name] | BRIN | [timestamp col] | [e.g., Time-range scan] | [e.g., Low storage cost] |\n| [Table] | [idx_name] | Partial | [col] WHERE [cond] | [e.g., Active records only] | [e.g., Smaller index] |\n\nIndexes deliberately NOT created:\n| Table | Column | Reason not indexed |\n|---|---|---|\n| [Table] | [Column] | [e.g., Low cardinality — not selective enough] |\n\n---\n\n5. PARTITIONING STRATEGY:\n| Table | Partition Type | Partition Key | Partition Interval | Retention | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [Table] | Range | [e.g., created_at] | [e.g., Monthly] | [e.g., 24 months hot] | [Notes] |\n| [Table] | List | [e.g., region] | [e.g., Per region] | Indefinite | [Notes] |\n| [Table] | Hash | [e.g., user_id] | [e.g., 16 buckets] | Indefinite | [Notes] |\n| [Table] | None | N/A | N/A | N/A | [Reason partitioning not needed] |\n\nPartition DDL example:\nCREATE TABLE [table_name] (...)\nPARTITION BY RANGE ([partition_key]);\n\nCREATE TABLE [table_name]_[period]\n    PARTITION OF [table_name]\n    FOR VALUES FROM ('[start]') TO ('[end]');\n\nPartition maintenance:\n  - New partition creation: [e.g., Automated via pg_partman | Manual monthly] \n  - Old partition archival: [e.g., Move to cold storage after 12 months]\n  - Old partition drop: [e.g., Drop after 24 months per retention policy]\n\n---\n\n6. NORMALISATION DECISIONS:\nNormalisation level: 1NF | 2NF | 3NF | BCNF | Denormalised | Mixed\nChosen level: [Level] — [Reason]\n\nDenormalisation applied:\n| Table | Denormalised Field | Source | Reason | Trade-off |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [Table] | [Field] | [Source table] | [e.g., Avoid expensive join on hot query] | [e.g., Update anomaly risk — mitigated by trigger] |\n\nTables kept fully normalised:\n| Table | Reason |\n|---|---|\n| [Table] | [e.g., Write-heavy — normalisation reduces update overhead] |\n\n---\n\n7. DATA TYPE DECISIONS:\n| Table | Column | Chosen Type | Rejected Type | Reason |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [Table] | [Column] | UUID | SERIAL | [e.g., Distributed-safe — no sequence contention] |\n| [Table] | [Column] | TIMESTAMPTZ | TIMESTAMP | [e.g., Timezone-aware — avoids DST bugs] |\n| [Table] | [Column] | NUMERIC(10,2) | FLOAT | [e.g., Exact decimal — avoids float rounding errors] |\n| [Table] | [Column] | TEXT | VARCHAR(255) | [e.g., No meaningful length limit — TEXT is cleaner] |\n| [Table] | [Column] | SMALLINT | INT | [e.g., Max value 32,767 — saves storage at scale] |\n| [Table] | [Column] | JSONB | JSON | [e.g., Indexable, binary stored — faster queries] |\n\n---\n\n8. CONSTRAINTS AND INTEGRITY:\n| Table | Constraint Name | Type | Definition | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [Table] | [pk_name] | PRIMARY KEY | [Column(s)] | Unique row identifier |\n| [Table] | [fk_name] |