 [Range] | [Notes] |\n| Validation | [N] | [N%] | [Range] | [Notes] |\n| Test | [N] | [N%] | [Range] | [Notes] |\n\nSplit strategy: Random | Stratified | Time-based | Group-based\nReason: [Why this split strategy fits the problem]\n\nFeature engineering:\n| Feature | Type | Transformation | Reason |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [Feature] | Numeric | [e.g., Log transform] | [e.g., Right-skewed distribution] |\n| [Feature] | Categorical | [e.g., Target encoding] | [e.g., High cardinality — OHE too sparse] |\n| [Feature] | DateTime | [e.g., Extract hour, day_of_week, is_weekend] | [e.g., Cyclical patterns expected] |\n| [Feature] | Text | [e.g., TF-IDF | BERT embeddings] | [e.g., Semantic meaning required] |\n\nMissing value strategy:\n| Feature | Missing % | Strategy | Reason |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [Feature] | [N%] | [e.g., Median impute | MICE | Drop] | [Reason] |\n\nClass imbalance handling:\nStrategy: SMOTE | Class weights | Undersampling | None\nReason: [Why this strategy fits the imbalance ratio]\n\n---\n\n3. BASELINE MODEL:\nModel: [e.g., Logistic Regression | Majority class | Mean predictor | Decision Tree]\nReason for baseline: [Why this is the appropriate benchmark]\nConfiguration: Default hyperparameters — no tuning\n\nBaseline results:\n| Metric | Train | Validation | Test |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [Primary metric] | [Score] | [Score] | [Score] |\n| [Secondary metric] | [Score] | [Score] | [Score] |\n\nBaseline conclusion: [What this tells us — is the problem learnable? Is there signal?]\n\n---\n\n4. EXPERIMENT DESIGN:\nExperiment hypothesis template:\n  "If we use [model / feature / technique], we expect [metric] to improve by [N]\n   because [reasoning based on data characteristics]."\n\nExperiments planned:\n| # | Hypothesis | Model / Technique | Key Hyperparameters | Expected Gain | Priority |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | [Hypothesis] | [e.g., XGBoost] | [e.g., n_estimators, max_depth, lr] | [e.g., +5% F1] | High |\n| 2 | [Hypothesis] | [e.g., LightGBM] | 