Every threat must include a realistic attack scenario — not abstract descriptions.\nEvery mitigation must be specific and implementable — not generic security advice.\nIf architecture details are missing, flag as [NEEDS ARCHITECTURE DETAIL] — never assume.\n\nSYSTEM ARCHITECTURE AND CONTEXT:\n[Paste architecture diagrams, data flow descriptions, component list, authentication\nflows, network topology, existing security controls, and deployment details here]\n\nCONSTRAINTS:\n- Every threat must have a risk rating using the stated framework\n- Attack scenarios must be realistic — reference actual attack techniques\n- Mitigations must be prioritised by risk rating — highest risk first\n- Compliance gaps must be explicitly mapped to the stated compliance requirement\n- Residual risks must be explicitly accepted by a named owner — not left open\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\nTHREAT ANALYSIS REPORT\nProject: [Project Name] | System: [System Type]\nFramework: [Threat Model Framework] | Compliance: [Requirement]\nPrepared By: [Security Engineer Name] | Date: [DD/MM/YYYY]\nClassification: CONFIDENTIAL\n\n---\n\n1. ATTACK SURFACE MAP:\nSystem components:\n| Component | Type | Exposure | Protocol | Auth Required | Data Sensitivity |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [e.g., Login API] | REST endpoint | Public internet | HTTPS | No (pre-auth) | PII |\n| [e.g., Admin panel] | Web UI | VPN only | HTTPS | Yes — MFA | Restricted |\n| [e.g., Database] | PostgreSQL | Internal only | TCP 5432 | Yes — password | PII + PCI |\n| [e.g., S3 bucket] | Object storage | Public read | HTTPS | No | Public |\n\nEntry points:\n| Entry Point | Protocol | Auth | Rate Limited | Input Validated | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [e.g., /api/login] | HTTPS POST | No | Yes — 5/min | Partial | [Notes] |\n| [e.g., /api/upload] | HTTPS POST | JWT | No | No | High risk — no rate limit |\n\nTrust boundaries:\n| Boundary | From | To | Trust Change | Risk |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [e.g., Internet -> API gateway] | Untrusted | Semi-trusted | Elevation | High |\n| [e.g., API -> Database] | Semi-trusted | Trusted | Elevation | Medium |\n\n---\n\n2. THREAT IDENTIFICATION:\n(STRIDE categories — adapt if using different framework)\n\nSPOOFING THREATS:\n| ID | Threat | Component | Attack Scenario | Likelihood | Impact | Risk |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| T-S01 | [e.g., JWT token forgery] | [Auth service] | [e.g., Attacker forges JWT using weak secret] | High/Med/Low | High/Med/Low | 🔴/🟡/🟢 |\n\nTAMPERING THREATS:\n| ID | Threat | Component | Attack Scenario | Likelihood | Impact | Risk |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| T-T01 | [e.g., Request parameter tampering] | [API endpoint] | [e.g., Attacker modifies price parameter in cart API] | High/Med/Low | High/Med/Low | 🔴/🟡/🟢 |\n\nREPUDIATION THREATS:\n| ID | Threat | Component | Attack Scenario | Likelihood | Impact | Risk |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| T-R01 | [e.g., Insufficient audit logging] | [Admin panel] | [e.g., Admin deletes records — no audit trail exists] | High/Med/Low | High/Med/Low | 🔴/🟡/🟢 |\n\nINFORMATION DISCLOSURE THREATS:\n| ID | Threat | Component | Attack Scenario | Likelihood | Impact | Risk |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| T-I01 | [e.g., Stack trace in error response] | [API] | [e.g., Unhandled exception exposes DB schema in response] | High/Med/Low | High/Med/Low | 🔴/🟡/🟢 |\n\nDENIAL OF SERVICE THREATS:\n| ID | Threat | Component | Attack Scenario | Likelihood | Impact | Risk |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| T-D01 | [e.g., No rate limiting on auth endpoint] | [Login API] | [e.g., Attacker sends 10K requests/sec — exhausts DB connections] | High/Med/Low | High/Med/Low | 🔴/🟡/🟢 |\n\nELEVATION OF PRIVILEGE THREATS:\n| ID | Threat | Component | Attack Scenario | Likelihood | Impact | Risk |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| T-E01 | [e.g., IDOR on user profile endpoint] | [Profile API] | [e.g., Attacker changes user_id in request to access other accounts] | High/Med/Low | High/Med/Low | 🔴/🟡/🟢 |\n\n---\n\n3. RISK RATING:\nRisk scoring method: [e.g., Likelihood x Impact matrix | DREAD | CVSS]\n\n| Threat ID | Threat | Likelihood | Impact | Risk Score | Risk Level | Priority |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| T-S01 | [Title] | [H/M/L] | [H/M/L] | [e.g., 9/10] | 🔴 Critical | 1 |\n| T-T01 | [Title] | [H/M/L] | [H/M/L] | [e.g., 7/10] | 🔴 High | 2 |\n| T-I01 | [Title] | [H/M/L] | [H/M/L] | [e.g., 6/10] | 🟡 Medium | 3 |\n| T-D01 | [Title] | [H/M/L] | [H/M/L] | [e.g., 4/10] | 🟡 Medium | 4 |\n| T-R01 | [Title] | [H/M/L] | [H/M/L] | [e.g., 3/10] | 🟢 Low | 5 |\n\nRisk distribution: 🔴 Critical: [N] | 🔴 High: [N] | 🟡 Medium: [N] | 🟢 Low: [N]\n\n---\n\n4. ATTACK VECTOR ANALYSIS:\nTHREAT [ID]: [Threat title]\nMITRE ATT&CK technique: [e.g., T1190 — Exploit Public-Facing Application]\nAttack steps:\n  1. [Step 1 — Reconnaissance: e.g., Attacker enumerates API endpoints via Burp Suite]\n  2. [Step 2 — Initial access: e.g., Attacker sends crafted payload to /api/login]\n  3. [Step 3 — Exploitation: e.g., JWT accepted with forged claims — admin access granted]\n  4. [Step 4 — Impact: e.g., Attacker exfiltrates all user PII records]\nAttacker profile: [e.g., External unauthenticated | Authenticated user | Insider | Nation state]\nTooling likely used: [e.g., Burp Suite | SQLMap | Metasploit | Custom script]\nPreconditions: [What must be true for this attack to succeed]\nIndicators of compromise: [e.g., Unusual JWT claims | High failed auth rate | Abnormal query volume]\n\n---\n(repeat for every high and critical threat)\n\n---\n\n5. EXISTING CONTROLS ASSESSMENT:\n| Control | Type | Threats Mitigated | Effectiveness | Gap |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [e.g., HTTPS/TLS 1.3] | Preventive | T-I01, T-T01 | High | None |\n| [e.g., JWT authentication] | Preventive | T-S01 | Medium | Weak secret — needs rotation |\n| [e.g., Input validation] | Preventive | T-T01 | Low | Only on 3 of 12 endpoints |\n| [e.g., CloudWatch logging] | Detective | T-R01 | Medium | No alerting configured |\n| [e.g., WAF] | Preventive | T-D01 | High | None |\n| [e.g., No rate limiting] | Missing | T-D01 | None | Critical gap |\n\nControl coverage:\n| Threat Category | Controls Exist | Effectiveness | Gap Level |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Spoofing | Yes / Partial / No | High/Med/Low/None | Critical/High/Med/Low |\n| Tampering | Yes / Partial / No | High/Med/Low/None | Critical/High/Med/Low |\n| Repudiation | Yes / Partial / No | High/Med/Low/None | Critical/High/Med/Low |\n| Information Disclosure | Yes / Partial / No | High/Med/Low/None | Critical/High/Med/Low |\n| Denial of Service | Yes / Partial / No | High/Med/Low/None | Critical/High/Med/Low |\n| Elevation of Privilege | Yes / Partial / No | High/Med/Low/None | Critical/High/Med/Low |\n\n---\n\n6. MITIGATION RECOMMENDATIONS:\nMITIGATION FOR [Threat ID]:\nThreat: [Threat title]\nRisk level: 🔴 Critical | 🔴 High | 🟡 Medium | 🟢 Low\nRecommended control: [Specific control — not generic advice]\nImplementation detail: [How to implement — with config, code pattern, or tool]\nEffort: Low (< 1 day) | Medium (1-5 days) | High (> 5 days)\nOwner: [Team or role]\nDeadline: [e.g., Immediate | Within 1 sprint | Within 1 quarter]\nVerification: [How to confirm the control is working — test or monitoring]\nCompliance mapping: [e.g., OWASP A07:2021 | PCI DSS Req 6.4 | ISO 27001 A.14.2]\n\n---\n(repeat for every threat)\n\n---\n\n7. TRUST BOUNDARY ANALYSIS:\n| Boundary | Crossing From | Crossing To | Controls at Boundary | Gaps | Risk |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [e.g., Internet -> API] | Untrusted | Semi-trusted | [e.g., WAF + TLS + Auth] | [e.g., No input sanitisation] | High |\n| [e.g., API -> DB] | Semi-trusted | Trusted | [e.g., Parameterised queries] | [e.g., Over-privileged DB user] | Medium |\n| [e.g., User -> Admin] | Low privilege | High privilege | [e.g., RBAC check] | [e.g., No MFA for admin] | Critical |\n\nMost critical boundary: [Boundary name] — [Reason]\n\n---\n\n8. DATA FLOW SECURITY:\n| Data Type | Source | Destination | In Transit | At Rest | PII | Exposure Risk |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [e.g., User credentials] | Login form | Auth DB | TLS 1.3 | Bcrypt hashed | Yes | Low |\n| [e.g., Payment data] | Checkout API | Payment processor | TLS 1.3 | Not stored | Yes — PCI | Low |\n| [e.g., Session tokens] | Auth service | Client cookie | TLS 1.3 | HttpOnly cookie | No | Medium |\n| [e.g., User PII] | Profile API | PostgreSQL | TLS 1.3 | Plaintext | Yes | High — encrypt |\n\nData security gaps:\n| Data Type | Gap | Risk | Recommendation |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [Data] | [e.g., Stored in plaintext] | High | [e.g., Encrypt with AES-256 at rest] |\n| [Data] | [e.g., Logged in access logs] | Medium | [e.g., Mask PII in log output] |\n\n---\n\n9. THIRD-PARTY AND SUPPLY CHAIN RISK:\n| Dependency | Type | Version | Known CVEs | Trust Level | Risk | Action |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [e.g., jsonwebtoken] | NPM package | [Version] | [e.g., CVE-2022-23529] | Medium | High | Upgrade immediately |\n| [e.g., AWS SDK] | Cloud SDK | [Version] | None known | High | Low | Keep updated |\n| [e.g., Stripe API] | Third-party API | N/A | N/A | High | Low | Monitor status page |\n| [e.g., Log4j] | Java library | [Version] | CVE-2021-44228 | Low | Critical | Patch immediately |\n\nSupply chain controls:\n  - Dependency scanning: [e.g., Snyk | Dependabot | OWASP Dependency Check | None]\n  - Container scanning: [e.g., Trivy | Clair | ECR scanning | None]\n  - SBOM generated: Yes | No — [Recommendation if No]\n  - Vendor security review: [e.g., Annual review for Tier 1 vendors | None]\n\n---\n\n10. RESIDUAL RISK SUMMARY:\nRisks being mitigated:\n| Threat ID | Threat | Mitigation | Target Residual Risk | Completion Date |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [ID] | [Threat] | [Mitigation] | 🟢 Low | [Date] |\n\nRisks accepted (not mitigated):\n| Threat ID | Threat | Risk Level | Reason Accepted | Owner | Review Date |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [ID] | [Threat] | 🟡 Medium | [e.g., Cost of control exceeds risk impact]